    "openingCompanyPrologueSecondWind": "SECOND WIND",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheWritingOnTheWall": "THE WRITING ON THE WALL",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWhatWeLeftBehind": "WHAT WE LEFT BEHIND",
    "openingCompanyPrologueRaisingHer": "RAISING HER",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheDepartureRoster": "THE DEPARTURE ROSTER",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSomewhereToDock": "SOMEWHERE TO DOCK",
    "openingCompanyPrologueAWayToSurvive": "A WAY TO SURVIVE",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheCerberusHadBeenTheClaimSEscort": "The Cerberus had been the Claim's escort until the run she came home with her reactor shroud holed and half her crew in the clinic. Raiders, the report said, and never said whose. Fixing her would have cost more than she was worth, so the operator stripped her best guns, moored her out in the belt and stopped thinking about her. Years of drifting grit did the rest: her frame never sat true again, her drive ran rough, and everything aboard ate spares. You towed her in to the locks with an ore tug. The first time you lit her drive, the coils blew and took the inspection lamps with them. The second time, nothing at all. The days chalked beside her airlock went from twelve to five while you pulled coil out of a hauler that hadn't flown since before the Claim had a name.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheDepartureRosterIsInYourHandwriting": "The departure roster is in your handwriting. Castle's additions run down the margin in a smaller hand: fuel, seals, filters, one more person who needed a berth, then another. Near the bottom, in block capitals, Sabine Hale has added her escort section: fifteen names, two struck through. While you were checking the last pressure patch, someone painted SECOND WIND over the old registry and didn't sign it.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCorvusFillsTheNavigationDisplay": "Corvus fills the navigation display: working yards, steady freight, Hegemony patrols crawling along the lanes. You plotted for it before the Claim was out of sight, on the strength of one name. Now the relay finally answers, and Castle opens a thread that is years old and ends in the middle of an argument: Nessa Venn, Jangala.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueACargoHandSleepsAgainstTheBridgeHatch": "A cargo hand sleeps against the bridge hatch with her boots on. The crew take turns in the bunks that still hold pressure. In the hold, Sabine's twelve sleep in shifts beside their stacked rifles. Below decks are two wrecked Hermes shuttles and compartments you haven't dared put back on the power bus.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouCanLetGoOfTheChair": "You can let go of the chair, Commander. She's holding. I sent everyone I could spare to get some sleep. Half of them are in the galley instead, asking each other what Jangala's like. None of them have been past the Claim's beacon. I'm the only one aboard who's seen it, and that was a long time ago.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueISignedForEveryOneOfThoseCarriers": "I signed for every one of those carriers, Commander. Nine years of manifests, and I knew a reactor stack from a crate of ore. I told myself it wasn't mine to ask. That's the part I keep coming back to.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueEveryoneAboardHasAPocketfulOfScrip": "Everyone aboard has a pocketful of scrip, and it spends at one counter in the sector, and that counter's dark. Over the years I kept back a little in real credits, the kind that spend anywhere. Not much. It's what gets us a yard. Nobody else knows how little it is.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWeGaveHerTheLowerHabsAirPlant": "We gave her the lower habs' air plant to get her sealed. After that there was no going back down. If she hadn't lit on the third try, I'd have been standing in the dark with everyone asking me what next.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSabineDidnTAskIfThereWasRoom": "Sabine didn't ask if there was room. She asked where her people should stand. The two she struck off were down the lower shaft when it went dark. She hasn't said their names since, and I haven't asked.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueAnOldFriendIOweHerMore": "An old friend. I owe her more than she'll let me say. If she's still at Greywater Down, she'll find us a cradle. If she isn't, we're a long way from anyone else who owes me anything. I'll tell you the rest on the way down.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNessaVennWeRanOreTogetherBefore": "Nessa Venn. We ran ore together before she settled into the yards on Jangala. Once spent three days towing my dead freighter home and swore she'd cut me loose at every buoy. Never did. If she's still at Greywater Down, she'll find us a cradle. If she isn't, we're a long way from anyone else who owes me anything.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNessaAnsweredSheSHeldACradle": "Nessa answered. She's held a cradle for us, and she'll do the work for what I've saved: bunks and a proper fit, nothing more. After that we're forty-five people in a yard with an empty galley. We'll need work, Commander, and soon.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenGoAndGetSomeSleepYourself": "Then go and get some sleep yourself.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouWerenTTheOneWhoLeft": "You weren't the one who left.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenItStaysBetweenUsUntilWeLand": "Then it stays between us until we land.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSheLit": "She lit.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenNobodyElseGetsLeft": "Then nobody else gets left.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSendIt": "Send it.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTakeUsTo": "Take us to {0}.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCrewAboardSpendableCredits": "Crew {0} / 45 aboard / {1} spendable credits",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheAlarmAboveTheHatchHasFinally": "The hatch alarm stopped an hour ago. Castle still looks up at it whenever the drive changes pitch. Someone has wedged a folded shift roster under the navigation console to stop it rattling. Harker's Claim is several jumps behind you, and nobody aboard has said its name since the first.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueHarkerSClaimWasThreeWeeksHaul": "Harker's Claim was three weeks' haul from the nearest port, and the transplutonic ore in its seams was worth every day of it. Then the good seams thinned, and slowly the Claim stopped paying. The second shaft was \"suspended pending survey.\" The drill rigs went out on the carriers \"for refurbishment\" and never came back. The clinic lost its surgeon to a transfer nobody had applied for. Carriers came monthly instead of weekly, and left heavier than they arrived. The notice that finally went up in the canteen was two lines long and ended with a date.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheLastOreCarrierTookTheMine": "The date was when facility support would end: air, heat, power. The last ore carrier left eleven days before it, with the administrators and the payroll aboard. Passage for workers was offered, priced in credits nobody paid in scrip could raise. The rest of the Claim kept reporting for shifts until the ration counter stopped taking company scrip.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCreditsHeldForTheConversionFirstBoat": "{0} credits held for the conversion / first boat and squad stores prepaid",
    "openingCompanyPrologueConversionPaymentDueFromFleetFundsPreparation": "Conversion payment due from fleet funds / preparation stores prepaid",
