    "openingRefitTrackVEHICLE_BAY": "Vehicle bay",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYDEFICIT": "Vehicle bay",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYDEFICIT": "Company vehicles cannot deploy yet; no refit is offered.",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYRESTORED": "Vehicle bay",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYRESTORED": "Engine tuning (not yet offered).",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_I": "Turret calibration",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_I": "Turret calibration (not yet offered).",
    "openingRefitTierVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_II": "Field repair",
    "openingRefitEffectVEHICLE_BAYIMPROVED_II": "Field repair (not yet offered).",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_CALIBRATION": "A mech's fire control is only as true as the last time someone boresighted it, and on a gantry with dead consoles that means a sergeant with a sight picture and a wrench. A bench wired into the cluster lets the Lab align every mount to the targeting suite between drops. Link it to the tactical core and the pilots get its target sort as well, so the torso is already swinging before they have picked the next one.",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_COOLANT": "Mechs fight on flux, and what decides how long they can keep firing is how cold their sinks go into the drop. Right now we charge them from a hose line off the scrubber loop. A plant of its own on the gantry chills the charge properly, and the reactor overhaul gives it the power to go colder still.",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_ARMOR": "Mech plate comes out of the workshop in standard sheets and gets bolted on as it comes. A press beside the gantries lets the Lab shape and fit each section to its frame and lap the joints, so a round meets more plate where it lands. It needs the workshop's tooling to cut it and a frame that will take the press.",
    "openingRefitLoreMECH_REPAIR": "A damaged mech waits in its gantry until somebody has time for it, and every part comes off the workshop's queue. A standing crew with proper jigs turns a repair round in days instead of a week. With a rack of spares cut ahead of time, a mount shot off on the ground is a refit rather than a new build.",
    "openingRefitLoreVEHICLE_BAY": "The gantries can berth a vehicle as well as a mech, but the company cannot field its own yet. When it can, the bay gets its own refits: engine tuning, turret calibration and a repair line. Until then there is nothing here to buy.",
