    "lessonSpeaker": "CASTLE / COMPANY OFFICER",
    "lessonContinue": "CONTINUE",
    "lessonLater": "NOT NOW",
    "lessonEquipment": "EQUIPMENT",
    "lessonMechLab": "MECH LAB",
    "lessonBarracks": "BARRACKS",
    "lessonHeadquarters": "HEADQUARTERS",
    "lessonBriefing": "BRIEFING",
    "lessonOpenWayward": "OPEN WAYWARD",
    "lessonReady": "READY",
    "lessonFirstLiftTitle": "OUR FIRST LIFT",
    "lessonFirstLiftHandoff": "That job needs a boat, Commander; no truck goes into Mara''s depot. Come to the Boat Deck and we''ll patch a Hermes.",
    "lessonUnderstood": "UNDERSTOOD",
    "lessonRefitTitle": "A PROPER ISSUE",
    "lessonRefitHandoff": "You brought our people home, Commander. Wayline has offered one free equipment package. Come to Equipment and we'll choose it.",
    "lessonRefitSquad": "Choose the squad receiving this issue. Wounded marines keep their billets and can receive it too.",
    "lessonRefitCompare": "Two packages, one free transfer. Steady Line strengthens sustained fire; Forward Screen brings pulse weapons and Janus armor. Select one to see what would change.",
    "lessonRefitClaim": "Learn the selected package when you're satisfied. It's our one free transfer; the other can be learned later.",
    "lessonRefitIssue": "The specs are ours. Now issue the kit with the highlighted order. The Machine Shop fits learned equipment for free.",
    "lessonGantryTitle": "WAYWARD AT THE GANTRY",
    "lessonGantryHandoff": "Counterattack left us a Hound. Come to the Mech Lab and we'll fit her spare missile rack.",
    "lessonGantry1": "There she is: Wayward. Open her gantry and we'll fit the SRM rack that came with her.",
    "lessonGantry2": "Select an empty shoulder, then drag the SRM-5 Frag spare from stores onto it. Keep the nose chaingun.",
    "lessonGantry3": "Now drag the SRM off its mount back to stores, then drag it back on. A refit returns hardware to stores; it never destroys it.",
    "lessonGantry4": "Fit checked. Owning a walker doesn't put her on the ground: select Mech Support in the Junction briefing when the contract supplies heavy lift.",
    "lessonInvestmentsTitle": "SPEND WHERE IT HELPS",
    "lessonInvestmentsCopy": "We have some breathing room. Engineering shows ship repairs; the Boat Deck shows lift and refits. Both are optional. Keep enough stores to raise and replenish a second squad.",
    "lessonFormationTitle": "FROM ONE SQUAD TO TWO",
    "lessonFormationHandoff": "Junction asks us to hold several places at once, so we bring two full squads. Let's check the Barracks and put both under command.",
    "lessonFormationFound": "We need another formation. Raise Squad shows the stores bill and musters under the selected officer. Buy any missing Marines, supplies or food at a market, or choose Not Now if we can't afford it yet.",
    "lessonFormationAssign": "Both formations exist. Assign them from the commander card in Barracks, then include both in Assign Squads at the briefing.",
    "lessonFormationRecover": "We have two formations but fewer than two full squads ready. Use the wrench on a short squad card to fill its empty billets, then assign both and include them in the deployment.",
    "lessonFormationWounded": "We have two formations but fewer than two full squads ready. Nothing is vacant: our shortfall is wounded, and they keep their places. Let them recover, then assign both and deploy.",
    "lessonSecondTitle": "PREPARE A LARGER FORCE",
    "lessonSecondMinimum": "The launch minimum is two squads with four ready marines each.",
    "lessonSecondCheck": "Check this briefing’s deployment requirements before committing.",
    "lessonSecondSummary": "This operation recommends {0} marines. {1}\n\nFull squads aboard: {2}. Ready marines: {3}.\n{4}{5}",
    "lessonSecondBill": "\n\nOne new squad\n{0}\nFounding provides twelve soldiers and their starter kit. Assign the squad to a commander, then use Assign Squads here.",
