		"nexInvasionRequirements": "Company detachment and lift",
		"nexInvasionFlavor": "The company lands to take {0} from its garrison. The whole garrison stands against you: win the ground and the world changes hands. Retreat or lose and it stays with its owner.",
		"nexInvasionNotApplied": "The invasion's result could not be handed to Nexerelin. The market is unchanged; the company's losses stand.",

		# Arrival cinematic (cinematic_export.py timelines name these keys). Hail lines are keyed from their catalog
		# ids in jangala_arrival_hail.json (hail and Castle's lines alike) and must match its text.
		"jangalaArrivalSpeakerApproach": "JANGALA APPROACH",
		"jangalaArrivalSpeakerCastle": "CASTLE  /  SECOND WIND",
		"jangalaArrivalLockTitle": "JANGALA",
		"jangalaArrivalLockDetailSystem": "CORVUS  /  ",
		"jangalaArrivalLockDetailFaction": "HEGEMONY",
		"jangalaArrivalHail01": "Cerberus on the inbound lane, this is Jangala Approach. Your transponder reads a decommissioned mining escort. State your business in Corvus.",
		"jangalaArrivalHail02": "Jangala Approach, this is Second Wind. Civilian. Crew and families aboard, nothing for sale. We're expected at Greywater Down, private cradle Kilo Nine.",
		"jangalaArrivalHail03": "Corvus is under Hegemony customs. Declare any AI cores, harvested organs, recreational drugs or heavy armaments.",
		"jangalaArrivalHail04": "Nothing to declare, Approach. Ore dust and tired people.",
		"jangalaArrivalHail07": "Second Wind, you're cleared to Greywater Down on civilian corridor four. Keep your mounts cold and stay in the corridor. Patrol has your signature.",
		"jangalaArrivalHail08": "Corridor four, mounts cold. Thank you, Approach.",
		"jangalaArrivalCastlePlanetside": "We've got a few days planetside before we'll need to move along, Commander.",
		"jangalaArrivalCastleReels": "So much greenery and life... it's like the travel reels from the canteen.",
		"jangalaArrivalCastleYard": "Set us down in that fenced yard on the east side. Nessa called in a favour to get us a berth for refit. Best behaviour.",
		"jangalaArrivalCastleAllHands": "All hands, get some rest, see the sights, but keep your identification on you. We regroup at the yard tomorrow.",
		"jangalaArrivalCastleOwnWay": "Hard part starts now, Commander. From here, we find our own way.",
	"agreusArcTitle": "A SMALL WAR / HOUSE RUSK",
	"agreusArcWarrant": "CIVIL-SECURITY PROCUREMENT WARRANT: Recover the bonded service archive and sealed calibration kit at Low Quay. On successful return, retain the Recovered Specter refurbishment pattern. Rusk's bond guarantees the supplier's service files, calibration tooling and compatible surplus stock. This covers named Greyhook occupations within his concession under Ko Combine administration. It grants no planetary police commission, civilian seizure right, military procurement status or orbital-fire authority. Yard management and debt enforcement require a separate agreement; this job chooses neither. Learned patterns remain yours. Deploying accepts these terms; you may leave and return without a deadline.",
	"agreusArcWarrantBrief": "Castle: North Weir is working. Rusk now offers 30,000 credits and the Recovered Specter service pattern for the Low Quay recovery. Secure the records office, then escort the supplier's technician into the calibration cage. Eight seconds of protected work at each site authenticate the archive and release the kit. Cover its marked carrier back to the western egress. Drent Haulage crews hold the stores and may try to block the loading exit. Four constables cover our approach; bring your working tender and fitted boats. Nadi Orr's signed shortage list identifies clinic consignments among the diverted cargo; those belong to the clinic, not our equipment award. The stores are sealed; outside we use pressure protection. Losing the calibration load, or the technician before the kit is recovered, fails the job. Authenticated records survive withdrawal. A new mobilization funds replacement calibration material and personnel. The reward is a cargo card: learn it, then choose an Armory fitting. Nobody is refitted automatically.",
	"agreusArcYardTerms": "INSPECTION ADDENDUM: Secure Latchkey's dispatch house, tooling hall and operator entrance. Preserve the marked calibration machine. On successful inspection, retain the Recovered Arbalest refurbishment pattern under Rusk's supplier guarantee. No bombardment or fighter strikes: the machines, homes and heating service must survive. Clearing Greyhook does not authorize civilian seizure, new leases or debt collection. Custody remains unsigned pending a separate agreement. Deploying accepts this inspection only; the offer has no deadline.",
	"agreusArcYardBrief": "Castle: Rusk offers 36,000 credits and the Recovered Arbalest service pattern for a working inspection at Latchkey Yard. Secure dispatch first. The constables will hold our gains while we clear the tooling hall and operator entrance. Six seconds of uncontested company presence secures each site; enemy contact can take it back. Hold all three together while a living technician completes twelve uninterrupted seconds at the tools, covered by company infantry. The marked calibration machine must survive ordinary fire and blast damage. Lenna Saye has supplied machine labels and a safe route from the housing frontage. Voss's prize crews hold the yard and have a finite counterattack; workers are not targets. Bring three full squads if possible, fitted boats and your working tender. Rusk funds heavy lift for your active owned mech lance if available; no walker is supplied. Recovered Specter is useful, but regular issue can do this job. Sealed halls and pressure protection suit Agreus's airless surface. Lost tooling or both inspection technicians ends this attempt. A later mobilization explicitly funds replacement personnel and tooling refit, with the losses kept on record.",
	"agreusArcReferral": "Mara Venn: Tamsin Vale sent a reference after Morrow's departure and fleet handover. Baronet Elian Rusk needs a company and a working construction tender at North Weir on Agreus, in Arcadia. His concession operates under Ko Combine administration. Water Under Seal pays 26,000 credits on victory. Replenish your people and fitted boats before leaving Corvus; this optional work has no deadline.",
	"agreusArcBrief": "Castle: Rusk pays for the weir to work when we leave. Tor Edek's technicians handle the sealed coolant switches. Escort their repair load, clear both switching rooms and protect the reconnection. Bring your owned tender into safe working range and build a Vulcan road gun. Protect its builders while the constables inherit the hold. Expect Greyhook to contest the maintenance road; hold until Edek reports the work secure. Agreus is cold and airless: our regular infantry use pressure protection outside the sealed halls. Destroyed repair cargo or the loss of both technicians forces withdrawal. Rusk provides a new load and replacement party for a later mobilization. This local security contract grants no planetary police commission or orbital-fire authority.",
	"agreusArcSmallWarTerms": "HANDOVER TERMS: Seize Black Sluice's customs block, fuel-control house and dispatch pier, and hand the site to the agreed local custody party at fuel control. The marked fuel storage is a preservation objective: its controls are a seizure target, not something to destroy. No bombardment or fighter strikes. This breaks one Greyhook surface foothold and its levy route; it is not a commission against every pirate in Arcadia. Deploying accepts these terms; the offer has no deadline.",
	"agreusArcSmallWarBrief": "Castle: The lead from the Latchkey handover holds. Pell's recovered levy files carry a Drent Haulage dispatch order signed by Mika Drent. Its load numbers match Nadi Orr's shortage report and name Black Sluice's transfer schedule; local pilots confirm the service approach. Rusk offers 44,000 credits to take that foothold and hand it to local holders. Seize the causeway customs block first; the holders occupy what we actually take, starting with customs the moment it is ours. Then fuel control. The causeway runs between walled settling beds with no cover, and Drent Haulage works that transfer road. A support gun covers it; the sealed service galleries north and south are the way round. Prize crews and Berth Four cover dispatch. Take it and its transfer records, reclaim anything we lose, then escort the custody party into fuel control and hold all three sites while they complete the handover. The marked fuel tanks must survive ordinary fire. Agreus is airless: pressure protection outside the sealed halls. Losing the marked fuel infrastructure or the whole custody party fails the attempt; a later mobilization is a disclosed replacement and refit, with the loss kept on record.",
	"agreusArcAgreementCommon": "Both agreements keep Rusk's secured title under Combine administration, the yard's enforceable debt, the same core equipment rewards and the company's duty to remove Greyhook's coercive presence. Chapter 4, Terms of Protection, pays 32,000 credits and a Boarding Jack section card on either route; victory ratifies the signed agreement.",
	"agreusArcCustodyUndertaking": "Escort Rusk's appointed custodians and put access under their office. Association workshops operate through new leases and debt deductions.",
	"agreusArcCustodyBenefit": "Rusk funds a 12,000-credit premium, payable only with Chapter 5 victory. Later district escort work comes through his office.",
	"agreusArcCustodyCost": "Independent tool access ends. Lenna records the company's role and does not become its worker-side contracting contact. The court terms remain lawful and burdensome.",
	"agreusArcCompactUndertaking": "Escort a joint custody party and preserve inspected common-service access under a signed repayment schedule. Rusk appoints security; the association retains shop operation and auditable service allocation.",
	"agreusArcCompactBenefit": "Lenna Saye becomes the contact for later district escort work. The existing common workshop access continues.",
	"agreusArcCompactCost": "The company forgoes the 12,000-credit premium to fund the transition guarantee; that fully satisfies its contribution, with no further debit. Rusk accepts the agreement but records the company as an independent counterparty rather than his preferred enforcement contractor. Debt and security duties remain.",
	"agreusArcCastleComparison": "Castle: Both papers keep Rusk's title, the debt and the same equipment on either route; Greyhook still has to go. Custody is the money and Rusk's office: 12,000 credits if Black Sluice falls, his managers stabilize the schedules, and the benches go on lease with deductions. Lenna stops being our contact on the workers' side. The compact costs us that premium. Lenna becomes our contact for escort work, the shops stay common and inspected, and Rusk files us as an independent counterparty. Divided administration will rub. Neither changes how we fight or what we can buy, and nobody on that yard is universally grateful either way. Nothing is committed until you sign; we can leave this and come back.",
	"agreusArcSigningNote": "Signing is final: the other agreement closes. Defeat or a later retreat does not reopen it. Before signing, the company may instead decline further work; completed fees and learned or carried cards are kept.",
	"agreusArcDeclinedRecord": "The company has declined further Latchkey work before signing. Rusk's three completion fees and both recovered section cards stand. Custody stays a matter between House Rusk, the association and the Combine courts; no fourth commission will be offered.",
	"agreusArcSpeakerLenna": "LENNA SAYE / LATCHKEY YARD ASSOCIATION",
	"agreusArcSpeakerVoss": "SERA VOSS / GREYHOOK FLOTILLA",
	"agreusArcSpeakerVossOpen": "SERA VOSS / OPEN CHANNEL",
	"agreusArcSpeakerRusk": "BARONET ELIAN RUSK",
	"agreusArcLennaGate": "You have opened the gate. Before you hand over the keys, read who is allowed through it tomorrow. Those benches repair the weir's pumps as well as Rusk's cargo gear.",
	"agreusArcLennaLien": "Mara Venn says you broke a lien for Wayline on Jangala. Whose side is the lien on this time?",
	"agreusArcVossWarning": "Pell collected his share from that yard. Your new agreement leaves him nothing. I've told him to leave it. Plan for him not listening.",
	"agreusArcVossLast": "Keep the pier. I've lost worse berths.",
	"agreusArcRuskFamily": "I have written to my family. I would rather not have. They will answer, and they will want to know why they had to.",
	"agreusArcDrentLead": "Recovered levy file: a dispatch order signed by Mika Drent of Drent Haulage. Its load numbers match Nadi Orr's shortage lists and name Black Sluice's transfer schedule. The order is a document, not a sighting; it says where the loads went, not who will be waiting there.",
	"agreusArcPlaceNorthWeir": "NORTH WEIR",
	"agreusArcPlaceLowQuay": "LOW QUAY",
	"agreusArcPlaceLatchkeyYard": "LATCHKEY YARD",
	"agreusArcPlaceLatchkeyHandover": "LATCHKEY HANDOVER",
