	"agreusGuideRouteDefault": "Learn both recovered-suit cargo cards, then fit Salvage-assisted Section in the Armory.",
	"agreusGuidePrepOpen": "Signing commits one route and closes the other. You may instead decline further work and keep completed fees and cards.",
	"agreusGuidePrepSettled": "{0}: “{1}” Escort postings recur: two squads, fitted boats; each consignment is new freight and new people.",
	"agreusGuidePrepRatified": "Three full squads recommended, fitted boats and working tender. Take customs, fuel control and dispatch; preserve the marked fuel tanks. Optional owned mech.",
	"agreusGuidePrepSigned": "{0}: “{1}”",
	"agreusGuidePrepComplete": "Issued gear is unchanged. Already learned or carried cards satisfy the award; selling a card does not renew it. Recovered equipment is below military issue.",
	"corvusDustLedgerTitle": "The Dust Ledger",
	"corvusDustLedgerBriefing": "We have spent enough contracts reacting to their attacks. This time we choose where to go. The Sable Wake crew buys departure times from a broker on Asharu. Their inland counting house holds the dispatch archive. Seize the marked high-value target and return to the extraction point with the records. We need their buyers, not a fight with Asharu's authorities.",
	"corvusDustLedgerDebrief": "The archive names a listening post on Warion. Sable Wake has been matching our manifests to intercepted departure calls. Our own schedules are in it too, released under Teodor Prell's dispatch authority. The last batch is dated the week he left. He built Wayline. I don't understand why he would sell it, and I don't know who he sold it for. You brought back a target we can act on. Put your company in order; when you are ready, we can take that link away.",
	"corvusDustLedgerTarget": "Dispatch archive",
	"corvusBlindWatchTitle": "Blind Watch",
	"corvusBlindWatchBriefing": "Your work on Asharu gave us Sable Wake's listening post on Warion. We have the location, the approaches and a count of their watch. This is an operation we can prepare on our own terms. Plant charges at all three marked installations to disable its interception network. Your squads must cover the planters while the site's security force responds. This is a temporary raider outpost on barren ground, far from any colony. Expect a light local garrison; our route watch has ruled out outside reinforcements.",
	"corvusBlindWatchDebrief": "Their listening post is silent. You followed the records, reached their outpost and took away the equipment they used to watch our departures. We are choosing the next move now. The routing tables point to their dispatch compound on Garnir. That can wait while you account for your people and equipment. This contract is paid. Let the company have a moment with what it achieved.",
	"corvusColdAccountTitle": "A Cold Account",
	"corvusColdAccountBriefing": "We found their buyers on Asharu and blinded their listening post on Warion. Sable Wake's dispatch compound on Garnir is the last link. Secure the marked pirate dispatch records and transmit the proof. The Hegemony has an Onslaught in the area. Give its captain proof of pirate ownership, and we can get the Navy to finish this for us. Withdraw every surviving squad and your Hound to the marked extraction point. The Onslaught will take station beyond the eastern perimeter. Get clear of the marked bombardment area and reach your pickup. Your shuttles will return for the survivors while the batteries demolish the stronghold. Board as soon as they land. The operation ends when the last shuttle carrying your survivors leaves the area; Resolute will finish its work on its own orders. Expect fortified positions and better-equipped crews; you do not need to clear the entire garrison.",
	"corvusColdAccountDebrief": "The records proved the compound belonged to Sable Wake. Your surviving company is clear. Resolute has its proof and its orders; you are not required to wait on the Navy's timetable. You have broken Sable Wake's operation against Wayline in Corvus. Your company found the records, disabled their listening post and brought back the proof that released Resolute's guns. Those achievements belong to you. I mistook the Navy's interest for a partnership; it offered no promise beyond this operation. Wayline knows what your work is worth. Other crews will still work these lanes, and larger powers set their own terms. We have something to build on, and more reason to choose our contracts carefully.",
	"corvusFlavor": "{0}: {1}",
	"corvusRequirements": "{0} squads recommended. Minimum: two squads with four ready marines each. Up to four fitted company boats can ferry the selected force. Wayline provides heavy lift for your active mech lance; select Mech Support. No fighter cover or employer infantry.",
	"waylineSentenceJoin": " ",
	"corvusWaylineTitle": "WAYLINE / THE CORVUS ACCOUNT",
	"corvusIntroNoRoute": "Our dispatch records point beyond {0}.",
	"corvusIntroDelivered": "Dispatch has receipts for delivered loads: {0}. That is work Wayline can build on.",
	"corvusIntroLostLoads": "The lost loads remain on the ledger too.",
	"corvusIntroNoFreight": "No freight made it through. The depot is still ours, but this route has not recovered.",
	"corvusIntroRelayClosed": "The relay contract is closed. Its payment and your work remain on our books.",
	"corvusIntroTail": "When we met, Wayline was coming apart. You gave us room to act. See to your company first. The work on Asharu can wait until you are ready.",
	"districtEscortCampaignName": "District Escort",
	"districtEscortCampaignTerms": "Terms: {0} credits once, on delivery of this consignment with its party and your company at the western apron. No equipment award, premium, house promotion, MRB standing, stationing contract or faction commission; the signed agreement and its ratification are unchanged. Four district constables hold the apron. Two squads recommended; your fitted boats carry your selected marines. If the consignment or both of its party are lost, or the company withdraws, the job is unpaid and the next posting is a new consignment with new people.",
	"districtEscortCampaignRuskSender": "OFFICE OF BARONET ELIAN RUSK / CONCESSION SECURITY",
	"districtEscortCampaignRuskParty": "Rusk custodial clerk",
	"districtEscortCampaignRuskBrief": "Rusk''s office: Under the custody agreement, the concession ships its own freight on its own schedule. Consignment {0} leaves the Low Quay loading lane for the western apron with two of my custodial clerks, who sign it over at the gate. Raiders still work the freight lane; two pickets have been seen on it and more will come onto the lane once your boats are down. Meet the carrier, then keep it covered. My managers expect it delivered, not defended in place.",
	"districtEscortCampaignLennaSender": "LATCHKEY YARD ASSOCIATION / COMMON SERVICE DESK",
	"districtEscortCampaignLennaParty": "Association service delegate",
	"districtEscortCampaignLennaBrief": "Lenna Saye: The compact lets the benches ship common-service work without asking Rusk''s office for a lease. Consignment {0} is pump parts and recovered stock for the weir and the yard; two of our delegates travel with it and sign it over at the western apron. Raiders still work the freight lane. Two pickets sit on it, and more will come onto the lane once your boats are down. Meet the carrier at the loading lane and get it, and our people, across.",
	"districtEscortCampaignHistory": "Escort record: {0}. This posting is a new consignment with new people.",
	"districtEscortCampaignRequirements": "Two squads recommended; two selected squads with at least four ready marines each required. Up to four fitted company boats. Four constables and a two-person handover party. No tender or mech required.",
	"districtEscortCampaignDebriefWon": "{0}: The consignment is signed over at the apron. {1} credits paid. The next load is new freight and new people; post again when the company is ready.",
	"districtEscortCampaignDebriefLost": "{0}: The consignment did not arrive. No fee. Confirmed losses stay on record; the next posting is a new consignment with new people, not this load retried.",
	"waylineArcTitle": "WAYLINE / AN OPEN ROAD",
	"waylineProgressRelief": "CHAPTER 1 / 2 — RELIEF",
	"waylineProgressDepot": "RELIEF COMPLETE / CHAPTER 2 — THE DEPOT",
	"waylineProgressComplete": "RELIEF COMPLETE / DEPOT COMPLETE",
	"waylineIntroRelief": "Castle sent your particulars, and I've read them twice. I broker for Wayline, and since the spring I run it, because our director took a post off-world and somebody had to. A year ago we ran freighters between worlds. We lost three cargoes in a season and sold the hulls to cover them, so now we're drivers on one planet's roads, pooling what's left so nobody has to sell their truck as well.",
	"waylineIntroDepot": "The assault is broken. Recovered traffic logs put the raiders at our freight depot. You have bought us breathing room. Now clear the depot, so our drivers can go back to earning a living.",
	"waylineIntroComplete": "The depot is ours again. Dispatch can start moving freight. I've passed your name to the Independent brokers. When we met, I was trying to keep Wayline from coming apart. You gave us somewhere to rebuild. These are new postings from other crews.",
	"waylineBriefingOnPlanet": " on {0}",
	"waylineBriefingRelief": "Your squad starts beside Wayline''s truck behind the freight checkpoint{0}. Reinforce the checkpoint gate. Raiders will come up the freight and warehouse service roads. Wayline brings in its militia by shuttle. Break the assault and bring as many people home as you can.",
	"waylineBriefingCounterattack": "{0}: Their assault is broken. Recovered traffic logs identify the occupied Wayline depot{1}. Land at the western staging apron and advance with our militia through the freight gate, loading yard and dispatch warehouse. Our Hound, Wayward, is offline in the maintenance berth just beyond the gate. Secure the berth and keep a squad there while they bring its chaingun online. Use it for the push into dispatch and the defense that follows; direct control is optional. Win the depot and the walker is yours, including recovery and repair if it is knocked out. Clear the warehouse and hold company units inside for eight seconds. Then defend dispatch against two attacks entering along both service roads. Defeat the finite raider force and secure the warehouse to win. We provide one shuttle; your company needs lift for two sorties. You''ll be paid on success, and I''ll vouch for your company with Independent brokers. Let''s give our drivers their road back.",
	"waylineDebriefReliefLost": "Castle sent the report. This isn't how either of us wanted our first contract to go. The assault is still a threat, so I can't authorize the fee. Get your company in order before you try again; I can keep this job open.",
	"waylineDebriefDepotLost": "The depot is still in raider hands. Get your company ready. The contract remains open.",
	"waylineDebriefReliefWon": "The assault is broken. Recovered traffic logs point to our occupied depot. Your first Wayline payment is cleared. I put your company's name on the authorization myself. Castle has our line-support and scout-screen specs; choose one transfer in Barracks Equipment, with free fitting in your Machine Shop. We can talk about the depot when you're ready. I'd rather keep working with the people who answered this call.",
	"waylineDebriefDepotWon": "The depot is ours again. Dispatch can start moving freight. Your payment is cleared, and Independent brokers now have your name. We have a place to load, keep records and organize work again. One thing I can't account for: they left the strongroom alone and took the dispatch board, every route and every schedule on it. You gave Wayline an open road. Take time to put your own company in order; you have earned more than another emergency call.",
	"waylineDebriefAlliesAllLost": "None of our militia came home. We'll have to rebuild that watch.",
	"waylineDebriefAlliesSomeLost": "We'll see to the families of the militia we lost.",
	"waylineDebriefMarinesLost": "I'm sorry for your company's losses.",
	"waylineDebriefHoundAward": "Castle has filed Wayward's transfer: one repaired Hound and its chaingun, with empty missile mounts. Castle is waiting in the Mech Lab with a spare SRM-5 Frag rack and a fitting walkthrough. The chassis is in your Mech Bay; Wayline supplies heavy lift on the supply-route jobs.",
	"supplyRouteLabelConvoy": "CONVOY / BREAKTHROUGH",
	"supplyRouteLabelCapture": "CAPTURE / HOLD",
	"supplyRouteLabelOperation": "OPERATION",
	"supplyRouteJunctionName": "Open the Junction",
	"supplyRouteThunderName": "Thunder Run",
	"supplyRouteSecurityName": "Route Security",
	"supplyRouteJunctionTerms": "Mara Venn: Getting the depot back has put Wayline on its feet again, Commander, but our freight is still stuck at the junction. When we sold the freighters, a debt-recovery outfit called Varro bought part of what we owed, and they have taken the junction as security: a toll on our drivers at the Weigh Station, and three months of contracted loads impounded in the bonded warehouse. The civil authority on Jangala calls it a lien between two freight companies and will not touch it. Iona Serr, our dispatch coordinator, needs the junction opened. Capture Weigh Station, Freight Yard and Junction Dispatch together. Six militia hold your gains while the company advances. Talon Two, a contracted Mudskipper gunship, goes ahead of your company to work the trenches dug across the road. You're paid on success, and Iona opens our militia stores to you: one Trench-Clearing Issue card, the rifles, rocket tubes and grenades our people kept for exactly this. Then we run the freed loads through the corridor on Thunder Run.",
	"supplyRouteThunderTerms": "Mara Venn: The junction is open. Now we put freight through the corridor. Land at the staging apron, clear the roadside strongpoints at Dispatch Post, East Crossing and Outbound Gate. On our first arrival, an earlier unescorted hauler is already under attack; its local camera feed shows the danger. The loads freed at the junction wait at staging. Talon Two returns to give your company close air support after Dispatch is secured. We've hired more ground muscle for the final breakthrough: a heavy tank and two reinforced APCs. Clear Dispatch, then defend for 90 seconds; take East Crossing and defend for 120 seconds while small raider groups enter along the cross streets. Select an infantry squad and use DEFEND AREA to cover an approach. Eight militia anchor the gains and assemble two roadside machine guns if their crews reach the posts. Give your squads a new order when the dispatch window ends. Our three loads move in stages, with freight released at 45-second intervals during the final breakthrough. Beyond Outbound Gate, raiders hold a fenced inspection checkpoint with dug-in machine guns and rifle bays. The tank breaks that gun line; the APCs screen the crossing while the freight passes between them. Keep the road open for the convoy; raiders will try to cut off the column. Wayline is paying for the armored crews and vehicles; your company leads the advance. You're paid when the run is complete, with more for every carrier that gets through. Dispatch tracks every delivery and loss; if we have to pull back, we return for the remaining loads. Get at least one through and we can fund regular Route Security contracts.",
	"supplyRouteThunderPay": "Terms: Cr. 6,000, plus 4,000 per carrier delivered, up to 18,000, settled when the run is complete.",
	"supplyRouteSecurityTerms": "Mara Venn: Capture Power Yard, Freight Gate and Relay Hall, retaining the landing apron. Eight militia hold secured ground while your company pushes forward. A limited raider reserve will try to retake your gains. Wayline pays for each security job held.",
	"supplyRouteFreightLedger": "Freight ledger: {0}.",
	"supplyRouteRequirements": "2 squads recommended; at least 2 squads with 4 ready marines each. Up to 4 fitted company boats. Wayline provides heavy lift for your active mech lance; select Mech Support and call it onto clear ground. No fighter cover.",
	"supplyRouteRecoveryFreight": "The delivered loads are real work on Wayline's books again. Castle's report says every ambush sat on the loads worth something and let the rest go by. I want to know who saw those manifests. We can fund regular Route Security. Take time to see to your company; the next contract takes us off-world, to Asharu.",
	"supplyRouteRecoveryJunction": "You have opened the junction. We have ground to organize from. Sabine says they were dug in before your boats were down. Somebody told them we were coming. Iona has put a Trench-Clearing Issue card in your fleet cargo from our militia stores; learn it when you want it, nobody's kit has changed. Thunder Run will put our freight through the corridor once your company is ready.",
	"supplyRouteThunderClosed": "Thunder Run / closed",
