	"storyVeteransRequirements": "50+ marines, discretion",
	"storyVeteransFlavor": "A broker on the back-channel reached out — your name's getting around, and apparently that's worth something. The job is straightforward on paper: hit a specific cache, get out clean, no questions asked about what's inside. The pay is real money. The broker's name isn't.",
	"storyRecurringReliefFlavor": "A freight checkpoint is under bandit attack. Land on the rear apron, reinforce the gate, and eliminate the assault force, including groups approaching along both access roads. The employer provides militia and one shuttle. The posting covers this relief sortie; other militia crews continue to need help.",
	"storyRecurringCounterattackFlavor": "A local freight crew needs an occupied depot cleared. Join the militia advance from the western apron through the gate and loading yard into dispatch. Eliminate the depot guards; expect a reserve inside. The employer provides one shuttle. Independent freight crews pool their security funds for jobs like this.",
